{"title":"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given that<br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f4379bb54ace17da33dbb217a03ab804b4ee9fcf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}&amp;(1)&amp; x\\text{ and }y\\text{ are both integers between 100 and 999, inclusive;}\\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad \\\\     &amp;(2)&amp; y\\text{ is the number formed by reversing the digits of }x\\text{; and}\\\\     &amp;(3)&amp; z=|x-y|. \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"457\" height=\"68\" />\n</p><p>How many distinct values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are possible?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We express the numbers as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb9ab88cfa35b02e6b4320b7815cfec8fe75743.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=100a+10b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"150\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/0328cf1fadbb202f49037209b82d8ea3990e5e67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=100c+10b+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" />.  From this, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/261c7befa5a947fa1cfb7b6e79634752a424d59b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}z&amp;=&amp;|100a+10b+c-100c-10b-a|\\\\&amp;=&amp;|99a-99c|\\\\&amp;=&amp;99|a-c|\\\\ \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"316\" height=\"68\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are digits, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are both between 1 and 9 (from condition 1), there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02f7e7bb8f4e6de2cce2b41023334ae5c126dd7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{009}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> possible values (since all digits except <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed this way).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II\" title=\"2002 AIME II\">2002 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2002\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195617\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.047 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 126/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1775/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 134/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/1